1y46|v|To utter words or articulate sounds, as human beings; to express thoughts by words; as, the organs may be so obstructed that a man may not be able to speak. ; To express opinions; to say; to talk; to converse. ; To utter a speech, discourse, or harangue; to adress a public assembly formally. ; To discourse; to make mention; to tell. ; To give sound; to sound. ; To convey sentiments, ideas, or intelligence as if by utterance; as, features that speak of self-will. ; To utter with the mouth; to pronounce; to utter articulately, as human beings. ; To utter in a word or words; to say; to tell; to declare orally; as, to speak the truth; to speak sense. ; To declare; to proclaim; to publish; to make known; to exhibit; to express in any way. ; To talk or converse in; to utter or pronounce, as in conversation; as, to speak Latin. ; To address; to accost; to speak to.	o:vbu,57,5~vbu,57,5	s:1int,24,13~1int,24,13	d:aox,22,3;2eq,7,8~2eq,7,8;aox,22,3	D:txm,56,3;24gy,9,4~24gy,9,4;txm,56,3
