1y8g|v|To weigh or lay out; to dispose of; to part with; as, to spend money for clothing. ; To bestow; to employ; -- often with on or upon. ; To consume; to waste; to squander; to exhaust; as, to spend an estate in gaming or other vices. ; To pass, as time; to suffer to pass away; as, to spend a day idly; to spend winter abroad. ; To exhaust of force or strength; to waste; to wear away; as, the violence of the waves was spent. ; To expend money or any other possession; to consume, use, waste, or part with, anything; as, he who gets easily spends freely. ; To waste or wear away; to be consumed; to lose force or strength; to vanish; as, energy spends in the using of it. ; To be diffused; to spread. ; To break ground; to continue working.	o:1blz,43,10;zcl,42,11;2447,39,68;i9y,32,4;noi,31,3;17un,29,3;2bj5,26,7~2447,39,68;zcl,42,11;1blz,43,10;2bj5,26,7;i9y,32,4;17un,29,3;noi,31,3	s:205y,16,9;1int,15,11~1int,15,11;205y,16,9	d:ncc,22,3;2hq,9,3;23hz,7,11;2el,7,3;1mzo,3,3~23hz,7,11;2el,7,3;ncc,22,3;2hq,9,3;1mzo,3,3	D:24gy,17,11;1c8n,15,12;qd7,9,9~1c8n,15,12;24gy,17,11;qd7,9,9
